{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfbz3wfZ8Jkf7Kr966VfC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Item 05 is done and marked `[x]`. Nothing failed anywhere: no certified value changed and no false refutation turned up. The gate passes (1,345 MOSP tests, 110 pathwidth_solver tests).\n\n**The whole search, rewritten from the theorems.** I added `paper2/solver_fix_soundness.py`. It contains a second copy of the search with the two repairs written straight from the Lean statements. It uses only functions from `paper2/search_check.py`. In particular, the \"hereditarily definite\" test there works by listing every intermediate set, so the C and Python matching code are checked against an independent method. Each run is compared four ways: with the exact answer, with node soundness at every node it expands, with the C (answer and node count), and with the production Python.\n- **Coverage:** 17,431,232 runs over 52,592 graphs at 1–17 vertices, under all 64 rule settings. That includes every labelled graph up to 6 vertices, every 7-vertex graph, random graphs at 8–13, the known counterexamples, and 12,000 graphs from the hunt's counterexample-prone family at 12–17.\n- **Result:** zero wrong answers, zero lost nodes (51.5 M checked), and zero mismatches with the C or the Python.\n- **The check can tell the rule sets apart:** 4,203 of these runs come out differently under the published rules. So agreement with the C shows the C really runs the repaired rules.\n\n**Differential harness, with the new defaults.** I ran it on every certified instance, not a sample: 43,935 at 9–40 customers (1.76 M calls) and 1,231 at 50–75 (29,544 calls). It found zero disagreements, contradictions or witness failures, and no call hit its deadline. The independent small-instance oracle agrees on all 13,612 instances it can check.\n\n**Corpus.** `benchmarks.corpus` still reads 6,374 of 6,376 certified, and `solutions/` is unchanged against HEAD.\n\n**Not covered:** 76–125 customers. Item 04's paired refutations remain the only record there.\n\n**One thing to watch:** the committed `learning/data/ensemble/differential.csv.gz` shows +2.5% refutation nodes against today's run at n ≤ 40. Item 04's paired measurement of the repair's cost is +0.004%. So that file must come from older code and shouldn't be read as what the repair costs.\n\nThe write-up is the \"Item 05\" section of `paper2/solver_fix.md`, and the status line at the top of that file now records item 05's result. The results are in `paper2/data/solver_fix_soundness_*` and `paper2/data/solver_fix_diff{40,75}*`; I wrote nothing over the committed differential files. I added one test, `test_the_c_runs_the_repaired_search_as_the_theorems_state_it`, to `tests/test_repaired_rules.py`. PROGRESS.md is updated to 5/10. Nothing is committed, as instructed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":152,"cache_read_input_tokens":157381,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":152,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":718,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"82ba5f6e-ee95-4615-a9a5-6407d969cdf8","uuid":"e6b690b4-2b72-4359-880e-32c0f34fad29","timestamp":"2026-10-01T18:23:56.881Z","request_id":"req_011Cfbz3wCXg8FMroDXmuF45"}
